      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the heads up, I was wondering how this was used!\n\nAs far as I can find only the HIDL service uses it in AOSP: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:hardware/interfaces/vibrator/1.0/default/Vibrator.cpp;drc\u003dbf3bc86bea21d6d2ee504619d3e939b856d06850;l\u003d68\n\nThe reason I added this \"override\" is that \"vibrator.default\" is added by https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:build/make/target/product/handheld_vendor.mk, which is then included by default by Cuttlefish and other AOSP targets: https://cs.android.com/search?q\u003d%22handheld_vendor.mk%22\n\nSo, the override is a workaround to tell the build to essentially remove \"vibrator.default\" from PRODUCT_PACKAGES if we\u0027re using this Vibrator AIDL APEX.\n\nPerhaps the proper fix is to stop including \"vibrator.default\" in handheld_vendor.mk?",
